# Example CODEOWNERS — copy to .github/CODEOWNERS at the repo root.
#
# This file is what gives the exception registry teeth: only lock owners may
# merge changes to the pocket-zipper policy. It works together with two repo
# settings on the base branch (see docs/ci/github.md, "Trust: protecting
# .pocket-zipper/**"):
#   1. Make the `pocket-zipper` job a REQUIRED status check.
#   2. Enable "Require review from Code Owners" and "Do not allow bypassing the
#      above settings".
#
# Lock owners approve every change under .pocket-zipper/ — the leading and
# trailing slashes cover the directory and all subdirectories, so this governs
# both config.yml and exceptions.yml.
/.pocket-zipper/ @org/lock-owners

# Designating approvers: `@org/lock-owners` is a team in your organization — its
# members ARE the approvers, and editing team membership in the org settings
# adds or removes approvers without touching this file. A bare `@username`
# entry also works, but that person must have write access to the repository.
# Prefer team ownership so the roster can change without a CODEOWNERS edit.

# Protect the CODEOWNERS file itself so the policy space cannot be rewired.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @repo-owner